MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

shader_bindings(label, resources, sizes) builds every compute shader's
per-entry-point map: the resources' Vulkan bindings become the same-
numbered Metal slots, the prepared push constants ride 24, and the
runtime-sized arrays take their host-size word at 30 (Metal's buffer
attribute model tops out at 30 — 31 was the driver's out-of-bounds
assert). the rack's transfer, depth, upright and upright_image
translate through their own maps; the MSL carries [[texture(N)]] and
[[buffer(N)]] where the resources declare them.

display_transfer_compute_runs_and_copies_pixels: the transfer's MSL,
its compute pipeline state, and the compiled shaders' slots checked
against the rack's own declarations — the honest compute route the
display transfers ride.

142 tests green, the whole metal feature clean without it.
